--TEST--
A `?secret string` and a `??` over one are refused at `echo`, `print` and a serialiser, as a `secret string` is — `rule:security/secret-sinks-refuse`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A nullable secret is a union of `secret string` and `null`. Every sink asks
// whether any member is `secret`, so the `null` member opens nothing.
// `Core\Env::secret` and `Core\Session::getSecret` both return this type.
secret string $s = "hunter2";
?secret string $maybe = $s;

echo $maybe;
print $maybe;
echo $maybe ?? "none";
var $bytes = Core\Serialize::encode($maybe);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0790]: `echo` cannot print a `secret` value
  --> case.nvs:8:6
%A
error[E0790]: `print` cannot print a `secret` value
  --> case.nvs:9:7
%A
error[E0790]: `echo` cannot print a `secret` value
   --> case.nvs:10:6
%A
error: aborting due to 4 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
